.SH KEYS
In the Sway Desktop session with the default swaydesk shortcut profile (Super is the logo key). The
shortcuts key of config.toml picks another profile: i3, hyprland, niri or dwm (see swaydesk\-desktop\-config(1));
Super+F1 shows the keys of the profile in use.
.TP
.B Super
Show or hide the application grid.
.TP
.B Alt+Tab, Alt+Shift+Tab
Switch windows in the order of use.
.TP
.B Super+C, Super+V
The notification center and the clipboard history.
.TP
.B Super+Shift+E, Super+Shift+R
Screenshot and screen recording.
.TP
.B Ctrl+Alt+Delete
The session menu.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/swaydesk/config.toml
The desktop configuration: language (locale), accent color (accent), GTK and icon themes (gtk_theme, icon_theme), folder color (folder_color), cursor size in pixels (cursor_size, 16 to 96, default 24), file manager (file_manager), weather location (weather_location), holidays (holidays) and when the System popup shows the power profiles (power_profiles_in_system: auto, always or never; see swaydesk\-system\-popup(1)). The fonts come from the GTK system font.
Change it with swaydesk\-theme\-app(1) or swaydesk\-theme(1). Its [enabled] and [enabled.bar] tables turn
session components and bar modules off, and its shortcuts key picks the shortcut profile (see
swaydesk\-desktop\-config(1)).
.TP
.I ~/.config/sway\-dock/config.toml
The dock configuration.
.TP
.I /usr/libexec/swaydesk/
The helper scripts and the session (on Arch,
.IR /usr/lib/swaydesk/ ).
